  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...High pressure will maintain fair weather and \na gradual warming trend through Saturday.\n\nClear skies and light winds tonight will be favorable for strong \nradiational cooling, and result in another cool night. Temperatures \nin the mid 30s are likely across the Tug Hill region with patchy \nfrost, and low to mid 40s elsewhere. A few of the normally colder \nspots across the Southern Tier, Finger Lakes, and other rural areas \nmay drop into the upper 30s as well. Otherwise, expect typical river \nvalley fog across the Southern Tier, with patchy fog elsewhere near \nbodies of water.\n\nCoastal low pressure maturing off the New England coast late this \nweek and into the weekend will cause surface high pressure centered \nover eastern Canada to gradually settle south across the region \nFriday before further pushing westward across the central Great \nLakes by Saturday. Overall fair weather will persist through the end \nof the work week and into the start of the weekend.",
